    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm stuck on my lit review. if i have a source with like 5 authors, how do i do the in-text citation for APA 7th vs chicago? i keep getting them mixed up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Most sources with multiple authors have their own specific rules, but in APA 7th you use a parenthetical list before the 3rd instance (Smith et al., 2020). Chicago has no such rule, so \"et al.\" only applies after the 2nd citation or when Footnote/Essay style requires one more author.  \nDon't rely on exceptions unless you know this is the style your textbook or professor specifies.  \nIf you mix them up you risk losing points, so make sure you know the exact author count for your first three citations.",
