    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "wait so for apa 7th it's just et al. from the very first time i cite them? i thought there was some rule about listing them all out first or something. can u clarify that specifically?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you are correct about APA 7th; however, it is only \"et al.\" starting from the **third** time you cite a work by the *same authors*, not the first time. You must list all authors for the 1st and 2nd citations (e.g., \"Fox et al.\" is wrong; it should be \"Fox, G., and H.\"). \n\nMost students remember the old rule where you listed everyone for the first couple of times, but APA 7th shortened this drastically to reduce clutter. \n\nTo avoid mistakes, simply check if you have cited that specific source twice before using the short form again.",
